    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **54 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points system.\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 added two static helpers:\n- `membershipPoints(Owner)`: starts at 0; `+2` email present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` when `householdSize >= 3`, `+3` when tenure exceeds 365 days.\n- `membershipLevel(int points)`: maps points \u2192 level (1 for 0\u20131, 2 for 2\u20133, 3 for 4\u20135, 4 for 6+).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 replaced the old inline `membershipLevel` expression (which capped at 4 via `Math.min`) with two mappings that populate `membershipPoints` and derive `membershipLevel` from those points.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipPoints` field and updated `membershipLevel` (now `maximum: 4`, points-derived description). The `OwnerDto` is regenerated from this spec at build time, so both fields are now returned in the response.\n\nLevel 4 remains reachable only via tenure (+3 \u2192 6 points), so a fresh owner with every other factor maxed scores 5 and stays at level 3, matching the spec and the Cp39 test.",
