    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:102`).\n\n## Before the method body runs\n\n1. **Security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must have `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`, else 403. (Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`.)\n2. **Request-body Bean Validation** \u2014 `@Valid` on the `OwnerFieldsDto`. Enforced *before* the body:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, letters-only pattern (up to 3 words, space/`'`/`-`), size 1\u201330\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, same pattern (trailing `.` allowed), size 1\u201330\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, must contain non-whitespace (`.*\\S.*`), size 1\u2013255\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, non-whitespace, size 1\u201380\n   - `postcode` (optional): 4 digits\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, size 1\u201320\n   - `email` (optional): `@Email`, size \u2264255\n\n## Inside the method body (in this exact order)\n\n3. **Map** DTO \u2192 `Owner` (`ownerMapper.toOwner`; id and pets ignored).\n4. **Normalize address** (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE) \u2192 **400** if empty after normalization; then set it.\n5. **Normalize telephone** to E.164 + **per-country national-digit-length check** (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210) \u2192 **400** on failure; then set it.\n6. **Normalize email** (lower-case) and set it.\n7. **Validate email domain** \u2014 reject disposable domains (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 **400**.\n8. **Validate postcode region range** vs city (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 **400**.\n9. **Future-date check** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is after the server date \u2192 **400**.\n10. **Default & roll registration date** \u2014 default to today if null, then **roll Sat/Sun forward to Monday** (business day); set it.\n11. **Daily rate limit** \u2014 count existing owners with that business date; if **\u2265100 \u2192 429**.\n12. Set `bulkSignupWarning = (todayCount > 80)`.\n13. Compute and set `householdId` (SHA-256 of normalized last name + postcode).\n14. **Identity-duplicate check** \u2014 if any existing owner shares the same `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) \u2192 **409**.\n15. **Household-duplicate check** \u2014 if household members already exist and `sharesHousehold != true` \u2192 **409**.\n16. **City cap** \u2014 if the city already has **\u226550 owners \u2192 409**.\n17. Set derived fields: `namesakeCount`, `householdSize` (members+1), `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`, `customerCode`.\n18. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`@Transactional`; Spring Data `save`). On flush, **Hibernate re-runs entity-level Bean Validation**: `@NotEmpty` on address/city/telephone/firstName/lastName, `@Pattern` E.164 on telephone, `@Email` on email.\n19. **Audit log** \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n20. **Set `Location` header** `/api/owners/{id}` and return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Steps 11, 14, 15, 16 each call `clinicService.findAllOwners()` \u2014 a full-table scan re-run for every check.\n- `addOwner` is **not** `@Transactional` itself, so each service call is its own transaction (the duplicate/limit checks and the save are not atomic together).\n- There are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist` etc.), **no** JPA auditing, and **no** application-event publishing. Every side-effect is coded explicitly in `addOwner` \u2014 the only persisted side-effects are the derived fields set in steps 4\u201317; the audit line and `Location` header are non-persistent."
